# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-addon-sqd` package. We use sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) to refine noisy samples taken from a quantum circuit that approximates the ground state of a chemistry Hamiltonian. Ground state energies are approximated by diagonalizing the Hamiltonian in subspaces formed by the refined samples.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menunjukkan contoh minimum yang berfungsi bagi pakej `qiskit-addon-sqd`. Kami menggunakan pepenyahpepenjuruan kuantum berasaskan sampel (SQD) untuk memperhalus sampel bising yang diambil daripada litar kuantum yang menghampiri keadaan asas Hamiltonian kimia. Tenaga keadaan asas dianggarkan dengan menyahpepenjuruankan Hamiltonian dalam subruang yang dibentuk oleh sampel yang telah diperhalus.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more explanatory end-to-end workflows that run on quantum hardware, check out the tutorials:\n"
msgstr "Untuk aliran kerja hujung-ke-hujung yang lebih terperinci dan dijalankan pada perkakasan kuantum, lihat tutorial berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Sample-based quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization): chemistry Hamiltonian workflow\n"
msgstr "[Pepenyahpepenjuruan kuantum berasaskan sampel](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization): aliran kerja Hamiltonian kimia\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization): fermionic lattice model workflow\n"
msgstr "[Pepenyahpepenjuruan kuantum Krylov berasaskan sampel](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization): aliran kerja model kekisi fermionik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs for SQD {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-sqd}"
msgstr "1. Sediakan input untuk SQD {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we define the chemistry Hamiltonian and quantum circuit that approximates its ground state. The system studied in this example is N₂ at equilibrium geometry in STO-3G basis with two core orbitals frozen. This system has ``8`` spatial orbitals and ``10`` electrons, which means the quantum circuit is defined on ``16`` qubits, where qubits ``0-7`` represent spin-up orbitals and qubits ``8-15`` represent spin-down orbitals. Since this is a closed-shell system with ``10`` electrons, we know each physically-valid sample should have hamming weight ``10``, where the hamming weight of both the left and right halves of the bitstring is ``5``.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kami mentakrifkan Hamiltonian kimia dan litar kuantum yang menghampiri keadaan asasnya. Sistem yang dikaji dalam contoh ini ialah N₂ pada geometri keseimbangan dalam asas STO-3G dengan dua orbital teras dibekukan. Sistem ini mempunyai ``8`` orbital ruang dan ``10`` elektron, yang bermakna litar kuantum ditakrifkan pada ``16`` qubit, dengan qubit ``0-7`` mewakili orbital spin-atas dan qubit ``8-15`` mewakili orbital spin-bawah. Oleh sebab ini ialah sistem lapisan tertutup dengan ``10`` elektron, kita tahu setiap sampel yang sah secara fizikal harus mempunyai berat hamming ``10``, dengan berat hamming bagi separuh kiri dan separuh kanan rentetan bit masing-masing ialah ``5``.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Generate noisy samples {#2-generate-noisy-samples}"
msgstr "2. Jana sampel bising {#2-generate-noisy-samples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a real workflow you would design an ansatz circuit, optimize it for hardware, and sample it on the QPU. Here we skip that and draw ``10,000`` uniformly random bitstrings instead. While our samples contain no information about the actual ground state, we will see that the SQD protocol can still recover the true ground state by iteratively refining these samples, diagonalizing, and using the energies at each iteration to inform the next round of bitstring refinement. We can eventually recover the exact ground state in this manner because the subspace containing the ground state is small enough to calculate exactly. Specifically, since we know each half of each bitstring (``8`` bits) should have hamming weight ``5``, we know the full Hilbert subspace of the system is size $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$.\n"
msgstr "Dalam aliran kerja sebenar, anda akan mereka bentuk litar ansatz, mengoptimumkannya untuk perkakasan, dan mensampelnya pada QPU. Di sini kami melangkaunya dan sebaliknya melukis ``10,000`` rentetan bit rawak seragam. Walaupun sampel kami tidak mengandungi maklumat tentang keadaan asas sebenar, kita akan melihat bahawa protokol SQD masih boleh memulihkan keadaan asas sebenar dengan memperhalus sampel ini secara berulang, menyahpepenjuruankan, dan menggunakan tenaga pada setiap lelaran untuk memaklumkan pusingan penghalusan rentetan bit seterusnya. Kita akhirnya dapat memulihkan keadaan asas yang tepat dengan cara ini kerana subruang yang mengandungi keadaan asas cukup kecil untuk dikira dengan tepat. Khususnya, memandangkan kita tahu setiap separuh bagi setiap rentetan bit (``8`` bit) harus mempunyai berat hamming ``5``, kita tahu subruang Hilbert penuh bagi sistem ini bersaiz $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Post-process with SQD {#3-post-process-with-sqd}"
msgstr "3. Pasca-proses dengan SQD {#3-post-process-with-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The objective of the SQD algorithm is to refine noisy samples taken from a QPU and ultimately diagonalize the Hamiltonian in a subspace spanned by those refined samples. This is done iteratively as follows:\n"
msgstr "Objektif algoritma SQD ialah memperhalus sampel bising yang diambil daripada QPU dan akhirnya menyahpepenjuruankan Hamiltonian dalam subruang yang direntangi oleh sampel yang telah diperhalus itu. Ini dilakukan secara berulang seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refine samples by postselecting only those which have correct particle number for both the spin-up and spin-down subsystems\n"
msgstr "Perhalus sampel dengan pascapemilihan hanya sampel yang mempunyai bilangan zarah yang betul bagi kedua-dua subsistem spin-atas dan spin-bawah\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonalize in small subspaces spanned by the refined samples and collect information about the subspaces that yield the the best (lowest) energies.\n"
msgstr "Nyahpepenjuruankan dalam subruang kecil yang direntangi oleh sampel yang telah diperhalus dan kumpulkan maklumat tentang subruang yang menghasilkan tenaga terbaik (terendah).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each iteration:\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap lelaran:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refine the noisy samples by probabilistically flipping bits in samples with incorrect particle number. The probabilities are calculated using the subspace information from the most recent diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Perhalus sampel bising dengan membalikkan bit secara berkebarangkalian dalam sampel yang mempunyai bilangan zarah yang salah. Kebarangkalian dikira menggunakan maklumat subruang daripada penyahpepenjuruanan terkini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonalize in small subspaces spanned by the refined samples\n"
msgstr "Nyahpepenjuruankan dalam subruang kecil yang direntangi oleh sampel yang telah diperhalus\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect information about the subspaces yielding the best (lowest) energies\n"
msgstr "Kumpulkan maklumat tentang subruang yang menghasilkan tenaga terbaik (terendah)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can see from the output that the algorithm converges to the exact ground state energy after ``6`` iterations and that the diagonalization is performed over the full Hilbert subspace of dimension $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$. Of course, diagonalizing over the full subspace is usually not feasible, and therefore, systems with ground states having sparse support are the most likely to benefit from subspace diagonalization techniques such as SQD.\n"
msgstr "Kita dapat melihat daripada output bahawa algoritma menumpu kepada tenaga keadaan asas yang tepat selepas ``6`` lelaran dan bahawa penyahpepenjuruanan dilakukan ke atas subruang Hilbert penuh berdimensi $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$. Sudah tentu, penyahpepenjuruanan ke atas subruang penuh biasanya tidak boleh dilaksanakan, dan oleh itu, sistem dengan keadaan asas yang mempunyai sokongan jarang paling berkemungkinan mendapat manfaat daripada teknik penyahpepenjuruanan subruang seperti SQD.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more information on the diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian function, visit the [API docs](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian).\n"
msgstr "Untuk maklumat lanjut tentang fungsi diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian, lawati [dokumen API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian).\n"
